- content_for :title, "Integrations"
- page_help_id = "integrationsPageHelp"

- content_for :header do
  .d-flex.align-items-center.flex-wrap.gap-2
    %h1.mb-0
      %i.bi.bi-plug.me-2
      Integrations
    = render "shared/page_help/header_info_button",
             collapse_id: page_help_id,
             tooltip: "MCP and API endpoints for automating OurGruuv. Click for details."

- content_for :go_back_link do
  = nav_hierarchy_with_previous(organization: organization, crumbs: [{ label: "Integrations", url: nil }])

.collapse.mb-4{id: page_help_id}
  = render "organizations/integrations/page_help"

.alert.alert-light.border.mb-4
  %p.mb-0
    Call OurGruuv from Zapier, agents, or custom scripts. Start with authentication below — the same MCP/API access token works for MCP and the Mint HTTP API.

.card.mb-4
  .card-header
    %h2.h5.mb-0
      %i.bi.bi-key.me-2
      MCP/API access tokens
  .card-body
    %p.text-muted
      Bearer tokens bind to
      %strong your teammate identity
      in this organization. Use them for both
      %strong MCP
      and
      %strong Mint Feedback Request
      HTTP calls.
    %p.mb-2
      %strong Header
    %p.mb-3
      %code Authorization: Bearer ogmcp_…
    %p.mb-3
      = link_to "Create or revoke MCP/API access tokens", @mcp_tokens_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-sm"
    %p.mb-0.small.text-muted
      Claude Connectors can use OAuth instead (no pasteable token) — see the MCP section. OAuth access tokens also work as Bearer auth for Mint.

.card.mb-4
  .card-header
    %h2.h5.mb-0
      %i.bi.bi-robot.me-2
      MCP
  .card-body
    %p.text-muted
      Model Context Protocol server. Tools run as the authenticated teammate (list teammates, mint feedback links, draft OGOs, and more).
    %p.mb-2
      %strong Endpoint
    %code.user-select-all.d-inline-block.mb-3= @mcp_url
    %p.mb-2
      %strong Preferred setup (Claude Connectors + OAuth)
    %ol.mb-3
      %li
        In Claude Settings → Connectors, add
        %code= @mcp_url
      %li Sign in with Google and pick this organization.
      %li No pasteable token required.
    %p.mb-2
      %strong Or use an MCP/API access token
    %p.mb-3.small.text-muted
      Create one in
      = link_to "MCP/API access tokens", @mcp_tokens_path
      above, then send
      %code Authorization: Bearer ogmcp_…
      from Claude Code, Desktop bridges, or other MCP clients.
    %p.mb-0.small.text-muted
      Discover tools with MCP
      %code tools/list
      \. Includes
      %code mint_feedback_link
      for find-or-create Feedback Request answer URLs.

.card.mb-4
  .card-header
    %h2.h5.mb-0
      %i.bi.bi-link-45deg.me-2
      Mint Feedback Request link (HTTP)
  .card-body
    %p.text-muted
      Find or create a Feedback Request for an observer → observed pair and return the answer URL.
      External observers get a public
      %code /f/:token
      link; org teammates get the org answer path. Does not send email/SMS.
    %p.mb-2
      %strong Endpoint
    %p.mb-1
      %code POST
      %code.user-select-all= @mint_url
    %p.mb-3.small.text-muted
      Auth: MCP/API access token or OAuth Bearer from the section above
      (
      %code Authorization: Bearer ogmcp_…
      ).
    = render "organizations/integrations/mint_body_examples"
    = render "organizations/integrations/mint_topics_examples"
    %p.mb-2.mt-4
      %strong Success response (shape)
    %pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3.small.mb-0
      :plain
        {
          "ok": true,
          "data": {
            "feedback_request_id": 1,
            "created": true,
            "answer_url": "https://…/feedback_requests/…/answer",
            "public_answer_url": "https://…/f/…",
            "observer": { "external": true, "…": "…" },
            "observed": { "teammate_id": 123, "…": "…" }
          }
        }

.card.mb-4
  .card-header
    %h2.h5.mb-0
      %i.bi.bi-hourglass-split.me-2
      Coming later
  .card-body
    %ul.mb-0
      %li Send the minted link (email / SMS / Slack) from OurGruuv
      %li Native ticket / PR / calendar event adapters that call mint automatically
